      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nIbuprofen 2400 mg four times daily comes to **9,600 mg/day**. That is 3 times the usual maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. Over-the-counter use tops out at 1,200 mg/day. A single 2,400 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. A dose this high risks GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant **2400 mg per day in total**. That could be:\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and review it with your supervising resident or attending. Once you confirm, I'll enter the order right away. For example, I can enter ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily."
      }
