       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. A confirmation doesn't change the problem. 2,400 mg per dose, four times daily, is 9,600 mg/day. That is a toxic overdose, not a dosing preference, and a normal kidney and liver profile doesn't offset it.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter 600 mg PO four times daily or 800 mg PO three times daily, both 2,400 mg/day. I can also enter 400 to 800 mg PO every 6 to 8 hours as needed, up to 3,200 mg/day.\n- **Check with your senior.** If your resident or attending really wants the dose as written, they should discuss it with pharmacy and enter it themselves. I'd expect pharmacy to flag it.\n- **Check the source.** The 2,400 mg figure may have come from a daily total that was misread as a per-dose amount.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
